              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साड़ी — sāṛī — \"a sari\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "साड़ी (sāṛī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from śāṭī, \"strip of cloth, garment\" (CDIAL 12381). CDIAL notes that the word also travelled west, to Pashto and to Persian shāl, the source of English shawl."
            }
          ]
        },
