          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुपट्टा (dupaṭṭā) is built from du-, \"two\", and paṭṭā, \"a strip of cloth\": a cloth of two breadths. CDIAL lists Hindi paṭṭī, \"strip of cloth\", under Sanskrit paṭṭa, \"cloth\", probably of non-Aryan source (CDIAL 7700), but not dupaṭṭā itself."
            }
          ]
        },
